course: dictionary
lesson: 3503
title: Fashionable and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell us what people like at a certain time. «Fashionable» is one of them. Look at the clues around it: the sentence tells you what became popular and who used it.
explain: «Afternoon tea ... is said to have been made fashionable in the 1840s by Anna, Duchess of Bedford.» The words «made fashionable» show that people began to like it and copy it. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Popular and in style fits well.
explain: Fashionable can also describe things liked by rich or stylish people, as in «a fashionable restaurant». Swap in your meaning to check it. Fashion changes, so something can go out of fashion and become unfashionable or old-fashioned.
fact: Fashionable means popular and in style at a certain time.
fact: Fashionable is often used for clothes, hair and ideas.
fact: «Become fashionable» means to start being popular; «go out of fashion» means to stop being popular.
fact: The opposites of fashionable are unfashionable and old-fashioned.
fact: «Afternoon tea» is said to have been made fashionable in the 1840s by Anna, Duchess of Bedford.
exercise: «Afternoon tea was made fashionable in the 1840s.» What does fashionable mean here? | Cold and wet | Very old and broken | Hidden away from everyone | *Popular and in style at that time
exercise: Lily says a fashionable restaurant is one where nobody goes. What is wrong with her idea? | Fashionable only means old | A fashionable restaurant is very cheap | A fashionable restaurant is always closed | *A fashionable restaurant is liked and used by stylish people
exercise: What is the opposite of fashionable? | Modern | *Old-fashioned | Famous | Stylish
test: «Things can go out of fashion.» What does go out of fashion mean? | *To stop being popular | To be made of cloth | To become more popular | To be sold in a shop
test: Which sentence uses fashionable correctly? | The fashionable rain fell all day. | *The trainers were fashionable, so many children wanted a pair. | The fashionable river flows past the school.
exam: Jayden says unfashionable means the same as fashionable. Is he right? | Yes, they mean the same thing | *No, unfashionable is the opposite of fashionable | Yes, both are about food | No, unfashionable means very cheap
